WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.246
Apple wants an

00:00:01.081 --> 00:00:02.201
AI agent that

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:03.050
uses your Mac

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:04.890
Bloomberg spotted an

00:00:04.702 --> 00:00:05.846
Apple job listing

00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:06.565
for a senior

00:00:06.365 --> 00:00:07.579
engineering manager

00:00:07.391 --> 00:00:08.204
to build an

00:00:08.051 --> 00:00:09.077
AI agent that

00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:09.478
can use a

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.032
computer

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:11.513
The posting says

00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:12.102
it browses the

00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:12.433
web

00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:13.706
works across apps

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:14.791
runs commands

00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:16.065
writes and debugs

00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:17.008
code and does

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.951
it all privately

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.319
Meanwhile

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.559
macOS 27.3 will

00:00:21.371 --> 00:00:22.467
warn users against

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:23.764
granting full access

00:00:23.576 --> 00:00:24.955
to third-party agents

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:26.170
as Anthropic

00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:27.715
OpenAI and Meta's

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.481
Muse push into

00:00:28.293 --> 00:00:29.118
the space

00:00:29.646 --> 00:00:30.660
Full story on

00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:31.367
the dashboard
